docs/markov_predictable_bound_validation_results.md-15-
docs/markov_predictable_bound_validation_results.md:16:The predictable arm escalated before onset in 53/4,000 alternative streams (1.325%); the fixed-bound comparator had none. Early escalations remain non-detections in the primary outcome. Dose intervals are descriptive and unadjusted across doses. Exposure sums the state-conditional expected cost contrast through the escalation event or last processed event; it is evaluator output, not observed prevented harm.
docs/markov_predictable_bound_validation_results.md-17-
docs/markov_predictable_bound_validation_results.md:18:This validation supports the registered history-only q process under this particular Markov-volatility model, where the conditional-mean null is exactly zero in each latent regime state despite persistent context and cost-square moments. It does not establish robustness to arbitrary dependence, delayed or informative labels, adaptive policies, repeated candidate selection, or interventions that alter outcomes. Query paths also differ between the fixed and predictable systems, so the result does not identify the eventwise bound as the sole cause of the gain. The method remains a standard predictable-bound e-process, with no novelty claim.
docs/markov_predictable_bound_validation_results.md-19-
docs/markov_predictable_bound_validation_results.md:20:See the [frozen design](markov_predictable_bound_validation_protocol.md), [full report](../outputs/markov_predictable_bound_validation/reports/validation_results.md), and [per-stream Parquet metrics](../outputs/markov_predictable_bound_validation/metrics/stream_metrics.parquet). No figure was generated because PaperBanana was unavailable in this environment.
--
