scripts/sota_sprint/fam_c.py-36-predictable coin. (iii) is optional skipping of a test supermartingale: under the pointwise
scripts/sota_sprint/fam_c.py-37-promotion null ``E[l0 - l1 | F_{t-1}, predictions_t] <= 0`` every recorded increment has
scripts/sota_sprint/fam_c.py:38:conditional mean on the null side, so Ville's inequality still applies. Under a non-stationary
scripts/sota_sprint/fam_c.py-39-alternative the CS then targets the average over *recorded* events, not over all events (the
scripts/sota_sprint/fam_c.py-40-same estimand change QCE records). No candidate reads the label of the event it decides on.
